<section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Tools</p><h1>Map tools</h1><p class="lede">Fast, accurate, private. Everything runs in your browser — your location never leaves your device.</p></div></section>
<section class="wrap grid-3">
  <a class="card card-link" href="distance.html"><div class="icon">↔</div><h2>Distance calculator</h2><p>Great-circle distance in km, miles and nautical miles, initial bearing, midpoint and estimated flight time.</p></a>
  <a class="card card-link" href="coordinates.html"><div class="icon">⌗</div><h2>Coordinate converter</h2><p>Convert between decimal degrees, degrees-minutes-seconds, UTM and geohash. Click anywhere to read coordinates.</p></a>
  <a class="card card-link" href="sun.html"><div class="icon">☀</div><h2>Sunrise &amp; sunset</h2><p>Sunrise, sunset, solar noon, civil twilight and day length for any place and date — including midnight sun.</p></a>
  <a class="card card-link" href="world-clock.html"><div class="icon">◷</div><h2>World clock</h2><p>Your own dashboard of time zones with live clocks, offsets and day/night indicators.</p></a>
  <a class="card card-link" href="antipode.html"><div class="icon">⊕</div><h2>Antipode finder</h2><p>Find the exact opposite point on Earth and whether it's land or ocean.</p></a>
  <a class="card card-link" href="../live.html"><div class="icon">◉</div><h2>Live Earth map</h2><p>Earthquakes, wildfires, storms, the ISS and the day/night line in real time.</p></a>
</section>
<section class="wrap prose"><h2>Accuracy notes</h2><p>Distances use the haversine formula on a sphere with the IUGG mean Earth radius (6,371.0088 km), which is accurate to within about 0.5% of the true ellipsoidal distance — more than enough for travel planning and education. UTM conversion uses the WGS84 ellipsoid with the standard Norway and Svalbard zone exceptions. Sunrise and sunset use the standard sunrise equation with atmospheric refraction (−0.833°) and are typically within one to two minutes of official almanac values; at very high latitudes errors grow. For surveying, navigation or legal boundaries, use certified professional tools — or <a href="../projects.html">hire a professional</a>.</p></section>
